<title>JAPAN: NGK Insulators to buy back own shares.</title>
<headline>NGK Insulators to buy back own shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's NGK Insulators Ltd said on Monday that it had decided to buy back up to 10 million of its own shares at a cost of 15 billion yen.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the move is aimed at boosting the efficiency of NGK's capital.</p>
<p>It will initially buy 9.5 million shares at 1,200 yen per share from August 27 to September 17.</p>
<p>Shares in NGK Insulators closed down 10 yen at 1,180 yen on Monday.</p>
</text>
